WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.411
- So Nicola, Justin have
y'all ever met each other?

00:00:03.411 --> 00:00:04.860
- No.
- No, never.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.693
- Never, oh my gosh

00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:06.791
- But good to meet you.

00:00:06.791 --> 00:00:08.747
Meet in quotes, good to meet you.

00:00:08.747 --> 00:00:10.042
- Yeah.
(host laughs)

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:12.880
- Justin, have you seen Bridgerton?

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.514
- I have, I've dabbled

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.500
and I agree with you.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.340
It's one of those things where

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.225
if you watch that show,

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:18.560
you gotta commit to it

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.260
because you're gonna be
sitting there for a while.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.614
- Yes.
- It's hard to

00:00:22.614 --> 00:00:24.190
get your eyes off of it.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.840
- Yes well also it sets a bar, Nicola

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.760
like by the end of it
I was a tad bit angry

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:31.784
because I was like,

00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:35.542
that's never gonna happen in real life.

00:00:35.542 --> 00:00:36.910
(laughing)

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.050
It's the most amazing,
whoa, it's really good.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:45.020
So if you've watched it then
you get where I'm going.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.220
Where are you calling
from right now Nicola?

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.050
- So I'm calling from
Galway, the west of Ireland.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.650
I'm actually in my mom's house right now

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.360
beside the fancy lamp.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.130
You know, you've gotta
show off the nice things

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.960
when you come on television.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.241
So I've been on lockdown
with my mom since March,

00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:02.720
since we wrapped Bridgerton pretty much.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.380
- Well, yeah, you would've
had to have taped that show

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.910
pre COVID cause no test yet.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.080
- There's not much social
distancing in Bridgerton

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.020
no it's very..

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.860
- Yeah, no testing in the
world would've covered that.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.160
But no, I love you and also
I have to mention this,

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.100
I love you in "Derry Girls" as well.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.040
The other Netflix show you--

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.050
- Oh my God.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.385
- Yeah it's so great.

00:01:23.385 --> 00:01:24.470
I love you in both.
- I did not know you've--

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.397
Oh, thank you so much.

00:01:25.397 --> 00:01:26.950
That's so kind.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.240
- Yeah--
- I mean very different shows.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.710
- Then that's what I loved as well.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.380
I loved that they were
completely different

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.370
and your personality in both are amazing.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.810
And you do a really great job of

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:41.680
kinda taking over the scenes
in the best way possible.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:42.840
I mean that in the best way possible

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.840
but were you performing as a kid?

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.180
- Oh, I loved it so much.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.330
My brother bought me a video camera

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.130
when I was about nine years old

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.640
and I became like a tyrant
making my own home movies

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.240
and getting my friends to
like do the "Spice Girls."

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.220
There we are doing "2 Become 1"

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.360
I was Pa spice,
(laughing)

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.631
and then my best friend
May was baby spice.

00:02:02.631 --> 00:02:03.970
(Nicola laughing)

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:06.020
And yeah, I was totally like a dictator

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.120
when it came to directing

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.330
and we used to recreate
episodes with friends

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.370
and all this kinda other
stuff, but we just, yeah

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.860
I loved it so much.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.949
- Oh man, I loved that too.

00:02:14.949 --> 00:02:16.200
I was the same kind of kid.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.430
We were always doing stuff like that.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.290
That was so embarrassing

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.850
that I would never want to show anyone.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:20.683
Whose dog was that?

00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:21.516
Which dog was that?

00:02:21.516 --> 00:02:22.472
Was that Paisley?

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:23.660
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.493
- That's Paisley.

00:02:24.493 --> 00:02:28.651
She's hey, it's COVID what do you want?

00:02:28.651 --> 00:02:29.952
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:29.952 --> 00:02:31.520
She's having moment, sorry.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.010
- No, I love it.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.902
- Am glad cause for a second
I was like, do I have a dog?

00:02:35.902 --> 00:02:37.098
(conversing indistinctly)

00:02:37.098 --> 00:02:38.140
But maybe I have a dog.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.093
- It's like a Wolf.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.730
She's like she needs the attention.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.347
Sorry, she's yeah--

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.530
- I pointed it out coz I think it's funny.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.260
I literally had to shoot in my
house this show at some point

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.720
and my dog, Henry, I was like,

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.660
he would just roam through the scene.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:54.400
I was like, well, okay.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.520
But Nicola, we also have
this picture you posted.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.993
Can you explain what's
what's happening here?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.260
- Yes, absolutely.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.220
So this was, I went to drama school

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.900
at the Oxford School of Drama

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.910
and people had to write
a list of what characters

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.360
they thought we'd be good at.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.260
And you know, there was like nerdy friend

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.810
which was Claire from "Derry Girls"

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.740
and there was walked over
person, Imperial drama,

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.300
which is Penelope in "Bridgerton."

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.600
So they got those right.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.277
And then one was like alcoholic,

00:03:18.277 --> 00:03:21.750
and am like, okay
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.490
Like maybe it's coz I
was the only Irish person

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:26.390
in the class and I
enjoyed drinking Guinness.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.939
Though they were like we
know what she is and yeah

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:30.270
(laughing)
- That's normal.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.103
- I haven't done that yet

00:03:31.103 --> 00:03:32.490
maybe that will be my next role.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.850
- I just love that person.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.560
Like, you know what you're
gonna nail, alcoholic.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:37.760
You're gonna nail that one.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.440
(laughing)

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.830
That's awesome.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.450
Well Nicola, congrats on
the success of Bridgerton.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.830
It's just taking over.
- Thank you.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:48.140
- How great though, is
the diversity on the show?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.270
That's what I loved about it mostly.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.360
- It's so incredible.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.070
I mean, it's a thing that

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.800
we haven't seen enough of
Imperial dramas, not even close

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.330
and it's a Shondaland land show

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.740
and Shondaland have done so much

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.010
in terms of diversity on television.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.020
So a period drum of theirs would be,

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:04.610
you know following in that path.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.450
And I think before the show came out

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:07.580
there were some naysayers

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.090
and people that were trying to like

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.010
download it on IMDB

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.930
because they didn't like
the fact it was diverse.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.910
But then we were watched
by 63 million households.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.130
So I'm like, well that shows

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.480
that people do like diversity on screen.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.618
There you go.

00:04:20.618 --> 00:04:23.340
- Yeah, it's so great.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.700
So true or false,

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.440
I heard that you stabbed
one of your co-stars?

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.240
So that's weird.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.030
- Unfortunately that is true.
(Nicola laughs)

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.710
So it was my first day on set

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.570
and it's quite terrifying getting a big

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:38.870
Shondaland Netflix job.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.880
You think I just don't
wanna screw this up.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:41.713
So they said to me

00:04:41.713 --> 00:04:43.650
you're very tiny, let's
let's put you in heels

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.960
and I thought, yeah

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:46.986
I'll do anything you want me to do.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.560
It became evident pretty quickly that

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.860
with the corset and the heels,

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.260
my balance was not so amazing.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:56.640
So I was walking along
and I fell three times.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.910
And the third time I was holding a parasol

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.110
which in the wrong
hands is a deadly weapon

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.460
and I fell forward and
stabbed Claudia Jesse

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.610
who plays Eloise Bridgerton in the hand

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.350
and she just started bleeding.
(laughing)

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:08.183
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:08.183 --> 00:05:09.016
- But she's still my friend.

00:05:09.016 --> 00:05:10.530
She's still my friend.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.460
But yeah unfortunately
there was a stabbing

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.020
on the first day and I was guilty.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.200
It was not good.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.870
- I mean, my thing is if I'm
wearing those long dresses,

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.120
anytime I'm on a stage
and it's a long dress,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.280
I look at my stylist and go,

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.050
I want the easiest shoes in the world,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.220
coz they can't even see your feet.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.330
So I don't even know why--

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.030
- Just throw yourself on the ground Kelly

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.060
that's all you need to do.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.107
Just be like, oh, throwing yourself over

00:05:33.107 --> 00:05:33.998
and then you'll never
have to wear heels again.

00:05:33.998 --> 00:05:34.831
- Yeah.

